-a7316f2a4a24","position":{"commit_sha":"96b61003f33cb2d9a2debd5c9959c05b14394c91","position":"1795035577787831621-00959b88-2dcd-4264-b118-a7316f2a4a24"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f4bff6a6cd8e89aa471c4cbf8177b5a296b75c32019b0e8ffde03316541bb152","event_uuid":"cccefff9-dcc4-4293-96d9-da7d5804b2f6","position":{"commit_sha":"994f4d7601ab7a871c16151e2d4c5828a69608ab","position":"1795039094718946200-cccefff9-dcc4-4293-96d9-da7d5804b2f6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"b0f43380aef47ca724ddd0434761f16587719c2fe73d52910d9ceab8f047c5c5","event_uuid":"67d5183b-551f-4828-9017-044db357c57d","position":{"commit_sha":"492fa827509850be07a6d25418fd057e96573bf3","position":"1795039125214036404-67d5183b-551f-4828-9017-044db357c57d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"38a1d0eecce128b021455dd368d69d8544daff2dc140fb04e8a5aaead7feb55e","event_uuid":"3907a976-c221-470d-82b0-5ca02176dbe3","position":{"commit_sha":"b0bc7a09232e2047e666983fdc4815c48d796e81","position":"1795039138615448266-3907a976-c221-470d-82b0-5ca02176dbe3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3424 merged as 9bef6894937 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, Linux ubuntu cells green, i.e. the case-sensitive filesystem). RED evidence: the new filename==prompt test failed on the pre-fix tree on macOS (string comparison, host-independent). make verify: 21,393 passed; 1 failed + 4 errors were all caused by my own `git add`/commit in the worktree mid-run (the repo-isolation guards reported HEAD moving 7e442645e5 -> 9bef689493 and the staged rename); those 5 test files rerun in isolation: 38 passed. Portability: case-only git rename (two-step through a temp name), string-compare test, workflow edit in a Linux-only job; Windows sweep dispatched as test.yml run 44390588952 on 9bef6894937.","timestamp":1795033514564105951},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Windows sweep confirmed: test.yml run 44390588952 on 9bef6894937, job `sweep (windows)` 135106845353 concluded success (2026-11-18 13:51 PST). The only failing job in that run, `sweep (py3.14t)` 135106845268, fails on test_mcp_idle_heap_release, which fails identically on every py3.14t run since 2026-11-17 and is unrelated to this rename; tracked as sediment-filched-icefish. Closing as preexisting: the misnamed spec file was a latent defect from when it was added.","timestamp":1795039094718946200}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794978434236791830,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"de366382-ff3a-4415-9a5f-81bfd0c50d5b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"77b6-868f-f4bd-461f"},{"link_uuid":"6f0a535d-a57e-4552-ac72-f394475194ba","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"afb2-a0bc-b3f8-456e"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-g7.eval.yaml` declares `prompt: plan-review-G7` (line 13), and it is the only packaged spec whose filename differs from its `prompt` field (checked over every `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml` at origin/main dd72b461814). `load_eval_spec(prompt_id)` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:71`) opens `<prompt_id>.eval.yaml` verbatim (`_packaged_eval_spec`, `eval.py:63`), and `calibrate_criterion(\"G7\")` maps the criterion to `criterion_prompt_id(\"G7\") == \"plan-review-G7\"`.\n\nSo on a case-sensitive filesystem (Linux, including the GitHub ubuntu runners):\n\n- `calibrate_criterion(\"G7\")` / `rebar criteria eval G7` raise `EvalError: no eval spec for prompt 'plan-review-G7' at .../plan-review-G7.eval.yaml: [Errno 2] No such file or directory`.\n- The `eval-live` loop in `.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml` takes `pid = spec[\"prompt\"]` (`plan-review-G7`) and calls `run_eval(pid)`, which raises the same uncaught `EvalError` and aborts the step before the specs that sort after it are run.\n\nmacOS's default case-insensitive filesystem hides it.\n\n## Evidence\n\nObserved in Gerrit change 3421 patch set 1 CI (GitHub run 44239093717, ubuntu py3.11/3.12/3.13 and eval-discipline): `tests/unit/test_eval.py::test_calibrate_criterion_opens_a_gate_session_for_its_solver` called `calibrate_criterion(\"G7\", ...)` and failed with exactly that `EvalError`; the same test passes on macOS. That test was switched to the `necessity` criterion so the change could land; the underlying mismatch is unchanged.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe spec file was committed under a lower-case name while every caller addresses it by its upper-case prompt id. The two other upper-case criterion specs (`plan-review-T10.eval.yaml`, `plan-review-T15.eval.yaml`) are already named after their prompt ids, so the established convention is \"filename == prompt field\", and G7 alone breaks it. Nothing tests that convention.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Rename the spec with a case-only `git mv` to `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-G7.eval.yaml` (two-step rename through a temporary name so it is recorded correctly on case-insensitive filesystems), and fix its header comment's `rebar prompt eval plan-review-g7` hint to `plan-review-G7`.\n2. Update the callers that relied on the lower-case name: `tests/unit/test_plan_review_g7.py` (`load_eval_spec(\"plan-review-g7\")`) and `tests/unit/test_eval.py` (`run_eval(\"plan-review-g7\", ...)`, three sites), and restore `test_calibrate_criterion_opens_a_gate_session_for_its_solver` to calibrate `G7`, the case that failed on Linux.\n3. Add a regression test in `tests/unit/test_new_eval_specs.py` asserting that, for every packaged `*.eval.yaml`, the filename stem (minus `.eval`) equals the spec's `prompt` field EXACTLY (case-sensitive string comparison, independent of the host filesystem), so a future mismatch fails on macOS, Windows and Linux alike.\n4. Make the `eval-live` loop in `.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml` survive one bad spec: wrap the per-spec `ev.run_eval(pid, ...)` in `try/except ev.EvalError`, print `::error::` naming the spec and the error, append the pid to `broken`, and continue to the next spec. The existing end-of-step `if broken: raise SystemExit(1)` still fails the job, so a bad spec is reported rather than hidden, but no longer skips the specs after it.\n\nRejected: a case-insensitive loader. It would need a directory scan per load, would make two specs that differ only by case ambiguous on Linux, and would hide the naming drift instead of fixing it.\n\n## Portability\n\nA case-only rename is handled by git on case-insensitive filesystems (macOS APFS default, Windows NTFS): checkout replaces the entry, and after the change both case-sensitive and case-insensitive hosts open `plan-review-G7.eval.yaml` by the exact name callers use. The new test compares Python strings, so it does not depend on host filesystem case behaviour. The workflow edit is inline Python in a Linux-only job and uses no OS-specific API. No subprocess, fd, path-separator or encoding behaviour changes.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-g7.eval.yaml` → `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-G7.eval.yaml` (rename + header comment)\n- `tests/unit/test_new_eval_specs.py` (new regression test)\n- `tests/unit/test_plan_review_g7.py`, `tests/unit/test_eval.py` (caller names; calibrate test back to G7)\n- `.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml` (eval-live per-spec error handling)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The packaged G7 spec is named `plan-review-G7.eval.yaml`, and `load_eval_spec(\"plan-review-G7\")` and `calibrate_criterion(\"G7\", ...)` load it (covered by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_g7.py` and `tests/unit/test_eval.py::test_calibrate_criterion_opens_a_gate_session_for_its_solver` passing in the Gerrit `Verified` ubuntu cells, which run on a case-sensitive filesystem).\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_new_eval_specs.py` contains a test asserting every packaged spec's filename stem equals its `prompt` field exactly; it fails against the pre-fix tree (RED) and passes after the rename.\n- [x] The `eval-live` step in `.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml` catches `EvalError` per spec, records the spec in `broken`, continues to the remaining specs, and still exits non-zero at the end when any spec is broken.\n- [x] `make verify` passes on the change, and the change lands through Gerrit with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","afb2-a0bc-b3f8-456e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"67d5183b-551f-4828-9017-044db357c57d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["evals","ci"],"ticket_id":"3a94-70a5-8c3b-4c66","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Eval spec plan-review-g7.eval.yaml is named in lower case but its prompt is plan-review-G7, so it cannot be loaded on case-sensitive filesystems","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6c4e485b-c576-4665-8085-25828bbed3b7","8ac3944f-4433-474b-8e12-453554f73265","8b71e661-56b